--TEST--
A property declared `void` or `never` is `E0742` at its type, with a default or without one, and no second error follows (`rule:types/grammar`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Holder {
    public void $nothing;
    public never $none;
    public void $withDefault = 1;
    public static never $shared = 2;
}

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0742]: `void` is a return type only, and this is a property
%A
3 |     public void $nothing;
  |            ^^^^ declared `void` here
%A
error[E0742]: `never` is a return type only, and this is a property
%A
4 |     public never $none;
%A
error[E0742]: `void` is a return type only, and this is a property
%A
5 |     public void $withDefault = 1;
%A
error[E0742]: `never` is a return type only, and this is a property
%A
6 |     public static never $shared = 2;
%A
error: aborting due to 4 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
